### Testing with Custom Inputs

Before submitting solutions, testing with custom inputs helps identify corner cases:

1. **Edge Cases to Test**:
   - Minimum possible values (e.g., $N = 0$, $N = 1$, negative numbers, `int.MinValue`).
   - Maximum constraint values (e.g., $N = 10^5$, checking for integer overflow or timeout).
   - Arrays with all identical elements or sorted in reverse order.
2. **Reading Variable-Length Inputs**:
   Reading lines until End-Of-File (EOF):
   ```csharp
   string line;
   while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) != null)
   {
       // Process line
   }
   ```

codeCard.code:
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string line;
        while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) != null)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;
            int n = int.Parse(line.Trim());
            Console.WriteLine(n * 2);
        }
    }
}

using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string[] inputs = Console.ReadLine().Split(' ');
        int a = int.Parse(inputs[0]);
        int b = int.Parse(inputs[1]);
        int c = int.Parse(inputs[2]);

        int maxVal = Math.Max(a, Math.Max(b, c));
        Console.WriteLine(maxVal);
    }
}

